conel:CMOS conel:belongsToModule "Camcorder"@en;
           a conel:SensorType;
           rdfs:comment """Complementary metal-oxide-semiconductor (CMOS) (pronounced \"see-moss\", IPA: /ˈsiːmɒs/), is a major class of integrated circuits. CMOS technology is used in microprocessors, microcontrollers, static RAM, and other digital logic circuits. CMOS technology is also used for a wide variety of analog circuits such as image sensors, data converters, and highly integrated transceivers for many types of communication. Frank Wanlass successfully patented CMOS in 1967 (US Patent 3,356,858).

(This description is partly based on or reuses content from the Wikipedia article \"CMOS\" (http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CMOS) and is licensed under the GNU Free Documentation License (http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/fdl.html).)"""@en;
